---
version: 2.0.2
title: analysis: invalid expression contexts
file: ./test/context_test.gleam
test_name: context_diagnostics_snapshot_test
---
Source:
module main
external Store from erlang "store" {
  load() -> Result(Int, String)
}
class User {
  new() { Store.load()? }
  get() { self.name }
}
f() { continue }
actor Counter {
  be increment() -> Int { 1 }
}

---
error: result propagation outside a function
  ╭─ src/main.pooka:6:11
  │
6 │   new() { Store.load()? }
  │           ──────┬──────
  │                 ╰─ this expression is not valid here
  ╰─

`?` must be inside a function or ordinary method returning Result. Constructors, behaviours, field initializers and tests cannot propagate a Result.

error: self outside a constructor
  ╭─ src/main.pooka:7:11
  │
7 │   get() { self.name }
  │           ──┬─
  │             ╰─ this expression is not valid here
  ╰─

Explicit `self` is only available during construction. Ordinary methods access fields and methods by name.

error: continue outside a loop
  ╭─ src/main.pooka:9:7
  │
9 │ f() { continue }
  │       ────┬───
  │           ╰─ this expression is not valid here
  ╰─

`continue` needs an enclosing loop in the same callable. An anonymous function cannot control its caller's loop.

error: behaviour result must be Nil
   ╭─ src/main.pooka:11:6
   │
11 │   be increment() -> Int { 1 }
   │      ────┬────
   │          ╰─ this expression is not valid here
   ╰─

An asynchronous behaviour has no reply value. Its result annotation may only be `Nil`.

Found 4 errors.

